      "source": [
        "# ML-Based Gradient Optimization and Predictive Maintenance with MADA Convergence\n",
        "\n",
        "This interactive Jupyter notebook demonstrates machine learning applications in the QED Vacuum Thrust Control system:\n",
        "- **Gradient Optimization**: Using TensorFlow to optimize magnetic gradients (e.g., ∇(h²)) for efficient thrust in magnetic circuits.\n",
        "- **MADA Convergence Optimization**: Optimize field vector directions to maximize convergence quality (NEW!).\n",
        "- **Predictive Maintenance**: Training a neural network to predict material degradation and adapt pulsing based on inputs including **MADA convergence quality**.\n",
        "\n",
        "**CRITICAL**: This demo shows how ML can detect and correct magnetic field misalignment (like the FreeCAD bug) automatically.\n",
        "\n",
        "Key libraries: TensorFlow for ML, NumPy for data handling, Matplotlib for visualization.\n",
        "\n",
        "Run cells sequentially. Adjust hyperparameters for experimentation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import sys\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import tensorflow as tf\n",
        "from tensorflow.keras.models import Sequential\n",
        "from tensorflow.keras.layers import Dense\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "# Add parent directory to path for imports\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.getcwd()), '..'))\n",
        "\n",
        "from simulations.equations import (\n",
        "    force_vector,\n",
        "    calculate_convergence_quality,\n",
        "    CONVERGENCE_OPTIMAL,\n",
        "    CONVERGENCE_WARNING,\n",
        "    CONVERGENCE_CRITICAL\n",
        ")\n",
        "from ai.navigation import MaintenanceNN\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Libraries imported successfully\")\n",
        "print(f\"TensorFlow version: {tf.__version__}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Part 1: Gradient Optimization in Magnetic Circuits\n",
        "\n",
        "Optimize the gradient ∇(h²) to maximize thrust F = χ B² ∇(h²) A ρ using gradient descent.\n",
        "We treat ∇(h²) as trainable variables and minimize a loss (e.g., -thrust for maximization)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Parameters (from equations.py defaults)\n",
        "CHI = 1e-10\n",
        "B = 50.0\n",
        "A = 1.0\n",
        "RHO = 1000.0\n",
        "\n",
        "# Initial gradient (3D vector)\n",
        "initial_grad_h2 = tf.Variable([1.0, 0.0, 0.0], dtype=tf.float32)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Optimizer\n",
        "optimizer = tf.keras.optimizers.Adam(learning_rate=0.01)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Loss function: Negative force magnitude (to maximize)\n",
        "def loss_fn(grad_h2):\n",
        "    F_vec = CHI * B**2 * grad_h2 * A * RHO\n",
        "    F_mag = tf.norm(F_vec)\n",
        "    return -F_mag  # Maximize thrust\n",
        "\n",
        "# Training loop\n",
        "losses = []\n",
        "grad_history = []\n",
        "for step in range(100):\n",
        "    with tf.GradientTape() as tape:\n",
        "        loss = loss_fn(initial_grad_h2)\n",
        "    grads = tape.gradient(loss, [initial_grad_h2])\n",
        "    optimizer.apply_gradients(zip(grads, [initial_grad_h2]))\n",
        "    \n",
        "    losses.append(-loss.numpy())  # Positive thrust\n",
        "    grad_history.append(initial_grad_h2.numpy().copy())\n",
        "    if step % 20 == 0:\n",
        "        print(f\"Step {step}: Thrust = {losses[-1]:.2e} N, Grad = {grad_history[-1]}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\nOptimized gradient: {initial_grad_h2.numpy()}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Final thrust: {losses[-1]:.2e} N\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot optimization progress\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
        "plt.plot(losses)\n",
        "plt.title('Thrust Optimization Over Steps')\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Step')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Thrust Magnitude (N)')\n",
        "plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Part 2: NEW - MADA Convergence Optimization\n",
        "\n",
        "**This is the critical addition that would have prevented the FreeCAD bug!**\n",
        "\n",
        "Optimize MADA field vector directions to maximize convergence quality.\n",
        "Starting from potentially incorrect directions, the optimizer finds the correct opposing configuration.\n",
        "\n",
        "Loss function: -convergence_quality (to maximize quality)\n",
        "Constraint: Field vectors should converge toward center point"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# MADA positions (fixed)\n",
        "mada1_pos = np.array([-0.3, 0.0, 0.0])  # Left side\n",
        "mada2_pos = np.array([0.3, 0.0, 0.0])   # Right side\n",
        "center = np.array([0.0, 0.0, 0.0])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Field magnitude (fixed)\n",
        "B_magnitude = 50.0\n",
        "\n",
        "# Start with WRONG configuration (both pointing away - the FreeCAD bug!)\n",
        "B1_direction_initial = (mada1_pos - center) / np.linalg.norm(mada1_pos - center)  # Pointing away!\n",
        "B2_direction_initial = (mada2_pos - center) / np.linalg.norm(mada2_pos - center)  # Pointing away!\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Initial (WRONG) configuration:\")\n",
        "print(f\"  B1 direction: {B1_direction_initial} (pointing away from center)\")\n",
        "print(f\"  B2 direction: {B2_direction_initial} (pointing away from center)\")\n",
        "initial_quality = calculate_convergence_quality(\n",
        "    B1_direction_initial * B_magnitude,\n",
        "    B2_direction_initial * B_magnitude\n",
        ")\n",
        "print(f\"  Initial convergence quality: {initial_quality:.3f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if initial_quality < 0:\n",
        "    print(\"  🔴 CRITICAL: Fields are DIVERGING (configuration error!)\\n\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"  ✓ Fields are converging\\n\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Trainable variables (unit vectors)\n",
        "B1_dir = tf.Variable(B1_direction_initial.astype(np.float32), dtype=tf.float32)\n",
        "B2_dir = tf.Variable(B2_direction_initial.astype(np.float32), dtype=tf.float32)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Optimizer\n",
        "convergence_optimizer = tf.keras.optimizers.Adam(learning_rate=0.05)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Loss function: Negative convergence quality + normalization penalty\n",
        "def convergence_loss_fn(B1_dir, B2_dir):\n",
        "    # Normalize directions\n",
        "    B1_norm = B1_dir / (tf.norm(B1_dir) + 1e-8)\n",
        "    B2_norm = B2_dir / (tf.norm(B2_dir) + 1e-8)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Create field vectors\n",
        "    B1 = B1_norm * B_magnitude\n",
        "    B2 = B2_norm * B_magnitude\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Convergence quality (dot product of normalized vectors, negated)\n",
        "    dot_product = tf.reduce_sum(B1_norm * B2_norm)\n",
        "    quality = -dot_product  # 1.0 = opposing, -1.0 = parallel\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Loss: negative quality (to maximize)\n",
        "    return -quality\n",
        "\n",
        "# Training loop\n",
        "convergence_losses = []\n",
        "quality_history = []\n",
        "B1_dir_history = []\n",
        "B2_dir_history = []\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Optimizing MADA field directions...\\n\")\n",
        "for step in range(100):\n",
        "    with tf.GradientTape() as tape:\n",
        "        loss = convergence_loss_fn(B1_dir, B2_dir)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    grads = tape.gradient(loss, [B1_dir, B2_dir])\n",
        "    convergence_optimizer.apply_gradients(zip(grads, [B1_dir, B2_dir]))\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Calculate quality for logging\n",
        "    B1_normalized = B1_dir.numpy() / (np.linalg.norm(B1_dir.numpy()) + 1e-8)\n",
        "    B2_normalized = B2_dir.numpy() / (np.linalg.norm(B2_dir.numpy()) + 1e-8)\n",
        "    quality = calculate_convergence_quality(\n",
        "        B1_normalized * B_magnitude,\n",
        "        B2_normalized * B_magnitude\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    \n",
        "    convergence_losses.append(-loss.numpy())\n",
        "    quality_history.append(quality)\n",
        "    B1_dir_history.append(B1_normalized.copy())\n",
        "    B2_dir_history.append(B2_normalized.copy())\n",
        "    \n",
        "    if step % 20 == 0:\n",
        "        status = \"✓\" if quality >= CONVERGENCE_OPTIMAL else \"⚠️\" if quality >= CONVERGENCE_WARNING else \"🔴\"\n",
        "        print(f\"Step {step}: {status} Quality = {quality:.3f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Final results\n",
        "B1_final = B1_dir.numpy() / np.linalg.norm(B1_dir.numpy())\n",
        "B2_final = B2_dir.numpy() / np.linalg.norm(B2_dir.numpy())\n",
        "final_quality = quality_history[-1]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\nOptimization complete!\")\n",
        "print(f\"\\nFinal (CORRECTED) configuration:\")\n",
        "print(f\"  B1 direction: {B1_final} (pointing toward center)\")\n",
        "print(f\"  B2 direction: {B2_final} (pointing toward center)\")\n",
        "print(f\"  Final convergence quality: {final_quality:.3f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if final_quality >= CONVERGENCE_OPTIMAL:\n",
        "    print(f\"  ✓ OPTIMAL: Fields properly opposing!\\n\")\n",
        "elif final_quality >= CONVERGENCE_WARNING:\n",
        "    print(f\"  ✓ ACCEPTABLE: Good convergence\\n\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(f\"  ⚠️  WARNING: Convergence could be better\\n\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Verify correction\n",
        "expected_B1 = (center - mada1_pos) / np.linalg.norm(center - mada1_pos)\n",
        "expected_B2 = (center - mada2_pos) / np.linalg.norm(center - mada2_pos)\n",
        "print(f\"Expected B1 direction: {expected_B1}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Expected B2 direction: {expected_B2}\")\n",
        "print(f\"B1 error: {np.linalg.norm(B1_final - expected_B1):.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"B2 error: {np.linalg.norm(B2_final - expected_B2):.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Visualization: Convergence Quality Optimization\n",
        "\n",
        "Plot showing how the optimizer corrects the field directions from diverging to converging."
